Rouge the rogue grew up in Redmonton, a rather redneck town
in the north. Of course, he was teased as a child, and then
as an adult, for his name. "I'll show you who's a spelling
troll!" he shouted, and headed off to the Dungeons of Doom
to prove his mettle. 

Rouge had a few special things in mind. He swore never to
exterminate another race of creatures, and true to his 
name, he would collect all the red items in the dungeon
that he found.

[Well, this is my 5th ascension in my reverse-alphabetical
order geas. Oddly, 'R'anger appears below 'r'ogue in the
class selection list. Rouge was to be genoless - since my
previous 4 all genoed L, h, ; and R if they could. 
Collecting red stuff was ideally meant to mean that the
starting sack would be named "things red" and every red
item would disappear - unID'ed - into the sack. An accident
with a ?oID giving full ID later IDed some red items, but
Rouge continued collecting the worthless pieces of red 
glass he found. I ended up without a red spellbook, though
I did polypile for one, and without a tin of red mold meat.
I only met two red molds the whole game though. Since I had
a wish left over at the end, I could have wished for one
of the two missing items. In Vlad's tower I finally found
a "oLS and decided that I was going to do without that as
well - spent the whole game with at most a "oReflection
around my neck. So much for conducts.]

[I didn't take many notes this game, so I can't narrate
much.]

Rouge spent _ages_ without decent armor and weapons.
The minetown altar was cross aligned, and his pet bit
it fairly early, and the next altar was on D15. The
mines did yield decent boots, kicking boots I think,
and dwarvish mithril, but these vanished again after
an encounter with a golden naga (or was it a lich?).
Rouge must have lost 4 or 5 good pieces of armor to
the nasties. In addition, Kos didn't seem to be very
quick with the artifact gifts - or with anything, really.
It took a long time before Stormbringer materialized.
First Orcrist, later Werebane and Trollsbane, I think.

Much gold was dragged around the dungeon. Got down to
AC 5 or so with gold given to the minetown priest
before chasing him away (convert altar, throw lots
of +1 daggers (didn't find many ?oEW at the beginning
either), then toss him a spare wand of digging). The
second priest, on D20, got Rouge down to a naked AC
of 0, but that was after Ludios, and after a pet 
troll claimed a refund, Rouge dragged some gold down
to the valley to end up at AC -2. Left some 70k
zorkmids in the valley.

D15, a co-aligned altar from the start, was the basis
for most of Rouge's operations. The portal to Ludios
was there too, that helped. Several chests were 
parked on cursed junk items (sometime I should create
rustproof cursed iron chains - or can Xorns still eat
them?) to sort out the loot. Much polypiling went on,
but it never produced anything really worthwhile,
except a wide variety of rings and amulets to be
IDed (and then tossed back on the pile if not
interesting). Poly & control were found this way,
and were to be most useful on the quest.

[O yeah, that reminds me of another conduct: no artificial
gain levels. So everything was done by collecting XPs
or polymorphing, never was a %oW or a !oGL quaffed (well,
one C!oGL to get out of the sanctum, but that was more
for effect). Rouge reached XP15 from hitting monsters,
and later polymorphs dropped him to 12 (after returning
from Xorn form in the quest) and raised him to 17 (after
trying to eat a "oMB and a =oIA, neither of which diffused
into his body, more's the pity).]

Medusa was D26, I think, the one with the round central
isle. This was reached long before Rouge had any way
of crossing the water, and also while he had an AC of 0
or so, since his helm and boots and gloves had disintegrated,
leaving him with chain mail and a dwarven cloak or so.

After finally retrieving a =oLevitation and a =oConflict,
Rouge returned to the castle, went in the back, killed
the dragons (darn, _still_ no silver or gray scales),
conflicted most of the monsters, retrieved the _cursed_
0:1 /WoW (ugh), and played mastermind from the inside to
lower the drawbridge. A disenchanter reduced his stock of
+1 daggers somewhat (there's no message, BTW, when thrown
items hitting a disenchanter are disenchanted), but he kept
11 around for dealing with things you want to keep at a 
distance - like mind flayers.

[O yeah, that was yet another conduct, inspired by a recent
thread on r.g.r.n: no spellbooks. It was OK to ID spellbooks,
but Rouge would read none of them - not even the red one.
The Dead one was ok to read, but only because you have to.
So all the mind flayers he ate were just for the stats,
since he wasn't spellcasting at all anyway.]

Sometime around now Rouge got tired of his pet troll getting
in the way of Stormbringer all the time, and abandoned him.
Later, a red dragon named Puff was tamed but promptly abandoned
afterwards. On Astral, some ants were tamed as buffer creatures,
but not to take with him to the bar.

With the castle wand, and already ID'ed scrolls of charging,
Rouge wished for a [GDSM (got "oR from Sokoban), [Dex (for
thieving, I guess), and a (MM. Wrote lots of ?oEA, really
worked at it for a while, checked spoilers, searched the
whole damn mines again for another dwarvish iron helm, 
and enchanted everything up as far as it would go. With
the extensive donating, this gave him an AC of -40 (would
go to -42 at the end after upping his elvish cloak from
+4 to +6). If it hadn't been for twoweaponing and never
finding a shirt, his AC could have been below -50, which
is something I've never had before.

The last wish (number 4) was for a (BoH, since that hadn't
turned up anytime either, and Rouge's oilskin sack and sack
named things red were getting heavy. Not once did he find
a lamp that lasted a long time.

In Gehennom, Rouge got bored and stood around taking a beating
from demons every now and then, hoping someone interesting would
show up, but noone did. Without magic mapping, it was a bit
tedious. He stumbled across the stairs to Vlad by accident
after digging down a few levels. In Vlad's tower, a sergeant
left a corpse and two K-rations. Rouge was hungry, so 'e', 'y',
and voila! He was a cannibal too. Oops. He didn't carry much
food most of the time, since slow digestion was on his finger
most of the time, and eating things for intrinsics kept
him almost satiated.

An early tengu had given him T-control, one of the few times
that one of my characters has gone out to eat leprechauns
and nymphs to get T-itis _after_ getting control. So that
was a way to get unsatiated fast. 

In the Wizard's tower, Rouge was glad he wasn't genociding
stuff, so the 'c's made effective weapons. Also an effective
weapon for the captain with leather gloves in the zoo there,
but a YASD from ages back had taught me how to deal with that
effectively. Rodney was stoned and the book retrieved.

Rouge walked all the way back to his stash on D15 to reorganize
before going to the Sanctum. Rodney came back twice in this time.
Oh well, +6 Stormy and a +4 saber polished him off fairly effectively.
Then back down down down, Sanctum. Grabbed another 'trice,
left a row of statues through the graveyard without waking anybody
(stealth is nice, certainly), offed the priests quickly, ditto
for the high priest, dropped the corpse and C!oGL to escape.
Fastest Sanctum run I've done so far.

Up, up, up, the mysterious force did get irritating at one point
when it threw me back on the same 4 levels about 5 times. One
double trouble, and up to the planes it was. Earth was straight-
forward, air was as well with a good stash of rings and good
AC, so it was just fly around and hit things. Fire took a little
while, but no Archons or other real nasties, what with Rouge
still being only level 17. Water was what I had saved the C?oGD
for, which made it a short run as well (I was wondering, I had
a greased cloak, and =FA, am I immune to grab attacks then? 
Can krakens pull me into the water there at all?), which left
Astral.


